1.179.m:
Aparājita said:
O king, a fearless man finds everything in the arms of the brave;
therefore, the destruction of the descendants of Raghu through valor pleases me.

Ajagara said:
Action for decoration brings prosperity when one has not conquered hosts of foes;
calamity is preferable to those decorations of prosperity that are not born of conquest.

Ruha said:
Fierce heroes look magnificent, like swelling breasts;
and for heroes as for breasts, battle brings scorn on the enemy.

Gadyu said:
Let weapons, broken and laughing mockingly when consumed, remain useless;
even if only one staff-like arm remains, who would tolerate defeat?

1.182.m:
I will tell of their chiefs; listen as I declare that to you: / Skanda, Viśākha, and likewise Naigameya; / Bhīma, Bhīmakara, Kravya, Nirata, and Krośa;
Kravyāda, and Havirbuddhi, Koṭimudgarika, Pṛthu; / Kāla and Upakāla, Siddhārtha, and Puṣpaka;
Puṣpamitra, Kokilaka, Siddha, and Lambodara; / Khalyū, Kapota, Lamboṣṭha, and Nāyāsa;
Yadaṇḍa, Gṛddhranāsa, and Gṛddhravṛttuka; / Kṣudraka, Kālakāla, Kāla, and Tatpuruṣa;
Vidyudbhūta, and Saṃvarta, Varta, and Āvarta; / Śitikaṇṭha, Kapardin, Kacchapa, and Parikaṇṭaka;
Pariprakāśa, Matta, and Mātaṅgavasana; / Gadarākṣa, Piśāca, Vīranāśa, and Valīmukha;
Mahābhūta, Nanda, Somānanda, Pramodaka; / Ānanda, Vyavasāya, Niścaya, and Parākrama;

Jaya, Vijaya, Sañjaya, and Kalpa; / Puṣpadanta, Dantavakra, Heguṇḍi, and Bhīṣaṇa;
Vasubhūti, Vasutrāta, Jīvaka, and Tāpasa; / Vīrabāhu, Subāhu, Sundara, and Gaṇḍa;
Tuṇḍā, Vicelā, Godanta, Kalaśa, Kalaśocara; / the seizing spirit Śīryagrāha, Lalāṭastha, Grīvāgrāhabharata;
Parilepaka, Jātyandha, Karāla, and Kuñjanāman; / Anyedyuka, Satataga, Traitīyaka, and Caturthaka;
Vyarocaka, Netraroga, and Kāsaśvāsānuga; / Dhūtapāpa, Pāpahita, and Pāpācāra;
Kāṇḍa, Dhanañjaya, Śaṭha, and Naiṣkṛtika; / Vasudhātṛ, Vasumanas, Gaura, Śotha, and Galagraha;
Bhrama, Cittamoha, and Kāryavighātaka; / Sarvakāryakara, Jṛmbhaka, and Āryaka.
